# Offer Review Format

Use this structure for every offer analysis under `offer/` (filename from
`.career-pipeline.yml` `naming.offer.analysis`, default `offer-analysis.md`):

```markdown
# Offer Review — <Company>

**Role:** <Job Title>
**Company:** <Company>
**Reviewed:** <date>
**Sources:** <paths or filenames under offer/, plus any chat paste notes>

---

## Recommendation: <Accept / Decline / Negotiate>

<2-3 sentence summary of the packet and primary reason>

---

## Compensation

| Component | Offer | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Base | ... | vs YAML floor / public comps |
| Bonus / other cash | ... or N/A | ... |
| Total cash (if stated) | ... | ... |

**Comps:** <brief comparable-role findings with cited public sources; flag uncertainty>

---

## Benefits

- **Strengths:** ...
- **Concerns:** ...

---

## Equity

Omit this section entirely when the packet has no equity/RSU/option language.

- **Quoted terms:** <verbatim from packet>
- **Vesting / cliffs:** ...
- **Competitiveness / concerns:** ...
- **Floor treatment:** apply `.career-pipeline.yml` `compensation.equity_counts_toward_floor` and optional `compensation.notes`

---

## Open Questions

- <bullets the user may want answered before deciding>
```

Read workspace-root `.career-pipeline.yml` (`compensation`, `preferences`) when judging floor fit and location/work-mode implications of the offer.
